# API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env.local and update with your values
#
# The frontend passes its API calls on to the backend at SETTING__BackendUrl.
# Leave it unset to use the backend on this machine, http://localhost:8042.
# SETTING__BackendUrl=http://localhost:8042
#
# Set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL only when the browser should call a backend
# elsewhere directly, instead of through the frontend.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# Backend API Authentication
# Set these in .env.local if your backend needs a key or token.
# Never commit real values.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_HEADER controls the header name (e.g. Authorization, X-API-Key).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_VALUE_PREFIX is the literal prefix prepended to the token
#   (include the trailing space if present, e.g. "Bearer ", or leave empty for raw keys).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_TOKEN holds the credential value.
#
# Note: NEXT_PUBLIC_* env vars are baked into the browser bundle. For production
# apps that talk to a real backend with sensitive tokens, prefer server-side
# authentication (token stays on the server) or a Next.js API route proxy. The
# values below are intended for local development against a dev backend — see
# authentication-intake.md.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_HEADER=Authorization
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_AUTH_VALUE_PREFIX=Bearer
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_TOKEN=
